# SwiftFormat configuration — MCP Router
#
# Deliberately conservative. Formatting rules that rewrite structure (rather than whitespace)
# create noisy diffs across a fleet of parallel runners, and a rule nobody agreed to is a rule
# that gets disabled the first time it fires on something important.

--swiftversion 6.0

# Match the documentation-comment style already used through the kit.
--maxwidth 110
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapparameters before-first
--wrapcollections preserve
--closingparen balanced

--indent 4
--trimwhitespace always
--stripunusedargs closure-only
--self remove
--commas inline

# `import` order is worth enforcing: it is mechanical and it removes a whole class of
# merge conflict between runners touching the same file.
--importgrouping testable-bottom

--exclude .build,DerivedData,build,node_modules,dist,.worktrees

# Structural rewrites are disabled on purpose. Both of these expand a readable one-liner
# (`var id: String { name }`, a guard that fits on a line) into three, which makes the diff noisy
# without catching anything. This file sticks to whitespace and ordering, where the tool is
# unambiguously right and nobody argues with the result.
--disable wrapPropertyBodies,wrapIfStatementBodies
